    {
      "id": "p0167-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "At first, the translator paralleled this wordplay by scrambling the word アンダーテイル (andāteiru, \"Undertale\") to create a new Japanese anagram: テアイダ・ルーン (teaida rūn, \"Teaida Rune\"). It’s unclear if the name holds any specific meaning, however, as teaida isn’t a standard Japanese word.",
        "raw": "At first, the translator paralleled this\nwordplay by scrambling the word\n7 / ')l''-f-1 Jv (andateiru,\n\"Undertale\") to create a new Japanese\nanagram: f-71'57''·1v-/ (teaida\nrun, \"Teaida Rune\"). It's unclear if\nthe name holds any specific meaning,\nhowever, as teaida isn't a standard\nJapanese word.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08747783,
          0.35908571,
          0.38323086,
