    {
      "id": "p0167-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Before Underta/e's Japanese release, Toby emphatically requested that \"Teida Rune\" be changed back to \"Delta Rune\" and left in English text. This choice preserved the original English anagram. For added measure, and for the Japanese audience's sake, the translator included the Japanese pronunciation of \"DELTA RUNE\" in parentheses the first time the term is introduced.",
        "raw": "Before Underta/e's Japanese release, Toby emphatically requested that \"Teida\nRune\" be changed back to \"Delta Rune\" and left in English text. This choice\npreserved the original English anagram. For added measure, and for the\nJapanese audience's sake, the translator included the Japanese pronunciation\nof \"DELTA RUNE\" in parentheses the first time the term is introduced.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09301918,
          0.53267143,
          0.69187288,
          0.61867857
        ],
